📊 Global AI Index: Measuring AI Leadership and Maturity Across Countries

I recently worked on a Power BI project using the Global AI Index dataset from Kaggle to analyze global AI leadership and understand what drives AI maturity across countries.

🔍What I Did

✔ Built an interactive Power BI dashboard covering 62 countries.
✔ Analyzed AI performance across three core pillars: Implementation, Innovation, and Investment.
✔ Studied key AI success drivers: talent, infrastructure, research, government strategy, and commercial adoption.
✔ Evaluated the impact of region, income level, and political systems on AI performance.
✔ Segmented countries into AI maturity groups: Power Players, Traditional Champions, Rising Stars, Waking Up, and Nascent.

🔍 Key Highlights:

📌AI leadership is driven more by implementation than innovation alone :
►Top countries consistently show stronger AI implementation capabilities than just research or investment.

📌Balanced ecosystems perform best : 
►Countries with both strong government strategy and commercial adoption outperform those focusing on only one area.

📌Economic and political factors matter :
►High-income regions and democratic systems lead in AI performance, while lower-income regions and restrictive regimes lag behind.

📌AI maturity is highly uneven globally : 
►A small group of countries dominate AI readiness, while most are still developing basic AI capabilities.

📌Rising Stars show strong growth potential :
►Countries like Israel, Singapore, and South Korea are close to joining the top AI leaders.

📌Waking Up countries show early progress in AI but lack consistency :
►Some countries in this group are close to becoming Rising Stars, while others are still building basic AI capabilities.

💡This project helped me strengthen my skills in Power BI, data modeling, DAX, and data storytelling, while improving my ability to turn complex datasets into clear, business-focused insights.

